# Ahlstrom polarizable water.
#
# P. Ahlstrom, A. Wallqvist, S. Engstrom, B. Jonsson,
# A molecular dynamics study of polarizable water,
# Mol. Phys. 68 (1989) 563.
#
# The charges give a dipole moment of 1.855 D, which is that of a water molecule
# on its own. A polarizable model is built this way on purpose: the enhancement
# of the dipole moment in the liquid is what the induced dipoles are there to
# supply, and charges already carrying it would polarize the water twice.
#
# The polarizability is one isotropic point of 9.718 a.u., which is 1.440 cubic
# angstrom.
#
# NOTE: Ahlstrom places that point at the centre of mass. It sits on the oxygen
# here, which is where a force field of one site for each atom can put it, and
# the two are about 0.065 angstrom apart. This is what an atom site
# implementation of the model does and it is not what the paper says.
#
# The sites are the atoms in the order a structure file gives them, the oxygen
# and then the two hydrogens. The hydrogens carry no polarizability.

@FORCEFIELD
name:  WATER
sites: 3
units: au

@MULTIPOLES
ORDER 0
3
1    -0.669000
2     0.334500
3     0.334500

@POLARIZABILITIES
ISOTROPIC
1
1     9.718000
